{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1188695-clarity-touchstone-questions","id":1188695,"title":"Clarity & Touchstone Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-22T16:15:30-08:00","id":1188695,"title":"Clarity & Touchstone Questions","content":"I have a few questions / clarifications I wanted to ask around about the Clarity and Touchstone rules:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>In the touchstones section it says as long as you have an attached Touchstone you subtract 2 from Clarity damage rolls. -3 with multiple, and add 2 with none. Are these all meant to apply to clarity attacks from breaking points, or just direct attacks on your clarity from other sources? I feel like the text implies the former but I would want it to be the latter, because I'm a little concerned breaking points will be all but meaningless at low Wyrd. Our game playing just had its second session, with I think five breaking points on characters with Wyrd ranging from 1-3. Every Clarity attack &quot;hit&quot; but only one resulted in actual damage, and that was <i>without</i> the -2 damage dice. With it we'd all be rolling chance dice for damage except our real wyrd-o who'd still only be rolling 1 die. Unless of course our touchstones get unattached, but that seems unlikely with virtually no damage ever getting through.</li> <li><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clarity section</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a changeling takes any more mild Clarity damage after her track is filled with damage of any kind, she [becomes Comatose]. If she takes severe damage after her track is filled with damage instead, [Comatose is persistent].</div> </div> </div> </div> Am I reading this correctly that you don't actually have to fill the track with Severe damage to inflict persistent comatose, and just taking a point of Severe while it's already full of Mild would do it?</li> <li>Another question from the above quote, if you take more damage from one hit than you have Clarity track left, do you fall Comatose immediately or do you have to actually take a fresh hit when it's already full?</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13075-malicwanderer","name":"MalicWanderer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}